252731,"year":2020},"elevation":409,"officialArea":40,"website":"http://kokand.uz/"},"summary":{"extract":"Kokand is a city in Fergana Region in eastern Uzbekistan, at the southwestern edge of the Fergana Valley. Administratively, Kokand is a district-level city, that includes the urban-type settlement Muqimiy. The population of Kokand as of 2022 was approximately 322,100. The city lies 228 km (142 mi) southeast of Tashkent, 115 km (71 mi) west of Andijan, and 88 km (55 mi) west of Fergana. It is nicknamed \"City of Winds\".","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4._%D0%A0%D1%83%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE-%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA_01.jpg/330px-%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4._%D0%A0%D1%83%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE-%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokand"},"twins":[],"climate":{"temp":[4.7,6.9,13.3,19.2,25.3,30.5,33,31.4,25.6,17.9,10.6,5.4],"rain":[17,23,26,23,21,13,5,7,4,14,24,22],"cloud":[73,75,68,61,53,42,36,34,32,46,60,70]}}